  "id": "Compound::DB00495 - Gene::55867",
  "verbalization": "Zidovudine, a nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor, is shown to bind to Slc22a6, a transporter involved in the transport of organic anions. This binding is further linked to the participation of Slc22a6 in sodium-independent organic anion transmembrane transport, and in inorganic anion exchanger activity. These pathways ultimately lead to the participation of Slc22a11, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Zidovudine influences the activity of Slc22a11. The evidence suggests that Zidovudine may modulate the function of Slc22a11 through interactions with Slc22a6, which in turn affects the transport of anions across cellular membranes. The integrated pathway highlights the role of Slc22a6 as a mediator in the interaction between Zidovudine and Slc22a11, with the observed scores indicating a plausible and consistent mechanistic link. The evidence supports a biologically plausible mechanism, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct effect of Zidovudine on Slc22a11.",
